<td id="Sx4.T3.7.4.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4.48</td></tr>
<tr id="Sx4.T3.7.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T3.7.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Full</th>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx4.T3.7.5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.99</span></td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center"><span id="Sx4.T3.7.5.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.02</span></td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.99</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.56</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.5.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">5.11</td></tr>
<tr id="Sx4.T3.7.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T3.7.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Rank 5</th>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.74</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.32</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.73</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">1.58</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.6.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.20</td></tr>
<tr id="Sx4.T3.7.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T3.7.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Rank 8</th>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">0.95</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.91</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.88</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">3.64</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.7.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center">4.37</td></tr>
<tr id="Sx4.T3.7.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx4.T3.7.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Rank 32</th>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">0.90</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.8.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">3.92</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.8.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="Sx4.T3.7.8.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.00</span></td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.8.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb">3.41</td>
<td id="Sx4.T3.7.8.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_bb"><span id="Sx4.T3.7.8.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.88</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Attention (Lin-only).</span>
Removing LoRA from attention and keeping it only in MLP/linear layers preserves seam closure (L–R Cons. = 0.99) but skews the motion profile:
Front/Back/Left/Right = 3.62/3.06/3.60/<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.48</span> (Table <a href="#Sx4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Ablation Study about LoRA Placement. ‣ Ablation Study ‣ Experiments ‣ PanoLora: Bridging Perspective and Panoramic Video Generation with LoRA Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>).
Qualitatively, this appears as stronger right-view displacement but weaker forward/backward progression, suggesting that linear-only adapters emphasize appearance/texture modulation over true camera/parallax motion.
In the frames, lateral edges (e.g., water/ground boundaries) shift more than the path expansion in front/back, while seams remain clean.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Linear (Attn-only).</span>
Removing LoRA from linear layers and keeping it only on attention projections likewise maintains near-perfect seams (L–R = 0.99) yet biases motion in the orthogonal direction:
Front/Back/Left/Right = 3.70/3.24/<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.12</span>/3.59.
Visually, the left-view lateral sweep is more apparent, but front/back trajectories advance more slowly than the default Full model.
This indicates that attention-only adapters mainly aid rotational/lateral alignment rather than depth-consistent forward motion.
Across examples, the <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 180^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 180^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> boundary stays closed, but parallax cues in front/back are reduced compared to the Full setting.
<br class="ltx_break"></p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.F5" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="Sx4.F5.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames_rank5.jpg" id="Sx4.F5.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/197;" width="698" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Rank 5</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="Sx4.F5.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames_rank8.jpg" id="Sx4.F5.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/197;" width="698" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Rank 8</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="Sx4.F5.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames_rank16.jpg" id="Sx4.F5.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/197;" width="698" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Rank 16</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_4">
<figure id="Sx4.F5.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames_rank32.jpg" id="Sx4.F5.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/197;" width="698" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Rank 32</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span><span id="Sx4.F5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank capacity threshold.</span> Ranks <math id="Sx4.F5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!8</annotation></semantics></math> underfit: seam breaks/repetitions and weak parallax (rank 5 worst; rank 8 partial recovery); rank 16 is most stable; rank 32 increases motion but introduces drift/flicker.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ablation Study on Rank Tuning.</h4>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We observe that
ranks <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!8</annotation></semantics></math> fail to produce geometrically valid panoramas. At rank 5, L–R Cons. drops to <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.74</span> with unstable motion (1.32/3.73/1.58/3.20), and the equirectangular wrap cannot close (visible discontinuities at <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 180^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 180^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>);
<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank 8</span> partially recovers (L–R = 0.95; 3.91/3.88/3.64/4.37) but still underperforms the default.
In contrast, the <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full (rank 16)</span> configuration yields the best balance (L–R =<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.99</span>; <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">4.02</span>/<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">3.99</span>/3.56/<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.11</span>) with coherent forward motion and sharp textures.
Pushing capacity to <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 32</span> increases motion (Back=<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.00</span>, Right=<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">5.88</span>) but reduces alignment (L–R=0.90), manifesting as semantic drift and temporal flicker.
Overall, <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 16</span> is the most stable choice; <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ranks <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!8</annotation></semantics></math></span> are underfit and fail to maintain global panoramic continuity.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.F6" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F6.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/different_rank_img/pe5_perspective_label.jpg" id="Sx4.F6.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/117;" width="698" height="117" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Rank 5</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F6.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/different_rank_img/pe8_perspective.jpg" id="Sx4.F6.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/117;" width="698" height="117" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Rank 8</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F6.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/different_rank_img/pe16_perspective.jpg" id="Sx4.F6.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/117;" width="698" height="117" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(c) </span>Rank 16</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F6.sf4" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/different_rank_img/pe32_perspective.jpg" id="Sx4.F6.sf4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/117;" width="698" height="117" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(d) </span>Rank 32</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 6: </span><span id="Sx4.F6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ranks <math id="Sx4.F6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!8</annotation></semantics></math> underfit</span>: at rank 5 the panorama breaks down (blurred/flat textures, weak parallax); rank 8 partially recovers but remains soft with limited depth cues.
<span id="Sx4.F6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rank 16</span> delivers the best balance—sharp structures and stable parallax.
Pushing to <span id="Sx4.F6.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 32</span> increases motion capacity but introduces drift/over-smoothness and geometric wobble.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Ablation summary.</h4>

<div id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Removing either branch alone preserves seam closure (L–R <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\approx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≈</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx</annotation></semantics></math> 0.99) but <em id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">biases</em> the motion profile: <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Attention</span> (Lin-only) favors appearance/texture modulation with weaker front/back progression, whereas <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">w/o Linear</span> (Attn-only) strengthens lateral/rotational alignment but reduces depth-consistent motion (Table <a href="#Sx4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Ablation Study about LoRA Placement. ‣ Ablation Study ‣ Experiments ‣ PanoLora: Bridging Perspective and Panoramic Video Generation with LoRA Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Using <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">both</span> components restores a balanced, 3D-aware trajectory with coherent parallax. Across ranks, a clear <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">capacity threshold</span> emerges: <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ranks <math id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!8</annotation></semantics></math></span> underfit (down to L–R=<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.74</span>), causing seam breaks and weak/unstable parallax (Figure <a href="#Sx4.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Ablation Study about LoRA Placement. ‣ Ablation Study ‣ Experiments ‣ PanoLora: Bridging Perspective and Panoramic Video Generation with LoRA Adaptation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>); <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 16</span> offers the best trade-off (L–R=<span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">0.99</span>; strong, balanced motion), while <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 32</span> increases motion but harms alignment (L–R=0.90) and induces drift/flicker. We therefore adopt the <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Full</span> placement at <span id="Sx4.SSx4.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">rank 16</span> as the default for robust panoramic video generation.</p>
</div>
<figure id="Sx4.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F7.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames5lr.jpg" id="Sx4.F7.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/162;" width="698" height="162" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(a) </span>Rank 5 — seam <em id="Sx4.F7.sf1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">not</em> closed; misalignment at <math id="Sx4.F7.sf1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm 180^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm 180^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> (L–R Cons. 0.74).</figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="Sx4.F7.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><img src="2509.11092v1/frames8lr.jpg" id="Sx4.F7.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:698/162;" width="698" height="162" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">(b) </span>Rank 8 — left–right seam aligned; panorama closes (L–R Cons. 0.95).</figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span><span id="Sx4.F7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of rank on left–right seam.</span>
Lower capacity (rank 5) cannot form a valid panoramic wrap, causing breaks at the <math id="Sx4.F7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\,\pm 180^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>±</mo><msup><mn>180</mn><mo>∘</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\,\pm 180^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math> boundary; increasing to rank 8 restores left–right alignment and a closed seam.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="Sx5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">Conclusion</h2>

<div id="Sx5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose a novel approach to panoramic video generation by reformulating it as a lightweight LoRA-based adaptation task, enabling efficient fine-tuning of pretrained video diffusion models. Our theoretical analysis confirms that LoRA can effectively model the perspective-to-panoramic transformation when its rank exceeds the task’s inherent degrees of freedom. Experiments demonstrate that our method achieves high-quality panoramic video synthesis with minimal training data, outperforming prior works in visual fidelity, consistency, and motion diversity. This work bridges the gap between standard and panoramic video generation, advancing immersive 3D content creation.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
